{"name":"Tavern","hex":"#b7a594","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tavern","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["New Inn Hall, Oxford, one of the earliest medieval halls of the University of Oxford."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tavern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tavern","blocks":[{"text":"A tavern is a type of business where people gather to drink alcoholic beverages and be served food, such as different types of roast meats and cheese, and where travelers would receive lodging. An inn is a tavern that has a licence to put up guests as lodgers. The word derives from the Latin taberna whose original meaning was a shed, workshop, stall, or pub."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Tavern_Scene-1658-David_Teniers_II.jpg/330px-Tavern_Scene-1658-David_Teniers_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tavern","wikidata":"Q154250"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Jan_Steen_-_Revelry_at_an_Inn_-_WGA21761.jpg/500px-Jan_Steen_-_Revelry_at_an_Inn_-_WGA21761.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Jan_Steen_-_Revelry_at_an_Inn_-_WGA21761.jpg/500px-Jan_Steen_-_Revelry_at_an_Inn_-_WGA21761.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Dutch tavern scene by Jan Steen, late 17th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJan_Steen_-_Revelry_at_an_Inn_-_WGA21761.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Raleigh_Tavern_elevation_%2810819427246%29.jpg/500px-Raleigh_Tavern_elevation_%2810819427246%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Raleigh_Tavern_elevation_%2810819427246%29.jpg/500px-Raleigh_Taver